    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0252" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.51/926.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Germany to the Secretary of
                        State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-06-06T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 6, 1912—1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Paris forwards your May 17 and May 24. The German Government is in accord with
                    your expressed views and has so informed the German banking group. Some
                    opposition is being shown by England and France, especially to Austrian
                    participation, and I believe that this is also shared by German bankers. The
                    German Government has expressed no views as to preliminary advances, their
                    disposition being to leave this question to the financial groups.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leishman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
